From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ad5xrecon <ad5xrecon@localhost>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 10:50:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] settings: Plugins overlay for the AD5X plugin system

A "Plugins" row in Settings > Printer (shown only where Klipper has the
ad5x_plugins object) opens an overlay listing the printer's plugins: the
installed ones with an on/off switch (Update and Remove for user-installed
ones), the catalog plugins not installed yet with Install, and a status
card with the running install/update job, its result and any warnings.
Switching, removing an enabled plugin and installing ask first, since
Klipper restarts; nothing can be changed during a print or while a job
runs. The object joins the status subscription so the rows follow the job
and are rebuilt after each Klipper restart.

Upstream: not applicable (AD5X OS specific)
